{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTraceLaw"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_H","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L209-L220","doc":"**And along every step above `n`**, by induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_step_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_step_span","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L197-L207","doc":"**Radical monotonicity along one filtration step, from spanning alone.**\n\nNo conditional expectation, no retraction: cyclicity, Markov, and the hypothesis\nthat `H (n+1)` is spanned by `H n` plus single sandwiches `v * g n * w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mem_rad_of_exhausted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mem_rad_of_exhausted","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L167-L175","doc":"**From one stage to the radical**, given that the stages exhaust `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_shiftedUpTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_shiftedUpTo","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L149-L165","doc":"**Orthogonality propagates up the filtration.**\n\nIf `a` is orthogonal to the stage `shiftedUpTo T 0 M₀`, it is orthogonal to every\nhigher stage.  `TowerSpan` supplies each step, `tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_sup`\nconsumes it.  This is the induction that makes one low-level computation settle\nevery level above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_sup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_eq_zero_of_mem_sup","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L130-L147","doc":"The sandwich step, extended from one sandwich to the whole span-plus-base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_sandwich_of_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_sandwich_of_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L111-L128","doc":"**The lifting step, and the reusable content of this file.**\n\nIf `a ∈ H n` is orthogonal to every element of a subalgebra `B ⊆ H n`, then it is\northogonal to every sandwich `v * g n * w` with `v, w ∈ B` as well.\n\nCyclicity moves `w` to the front, Markov strips `g n`, and `v * w` is back in\n`B`. So the radical relative to a stage of the filtration only ever grows — one\ncomputation at one level settles every level above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_gen_sub_z_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.tr_mul_gen_sub_z_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L102-L109","doc":"**The Markov axiom, read as orthogonality.**  The new generator arrives with\na prescribed component `z • 1`, and what is left over is orthogonal to the whole\nof the level below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.one_notMem_rad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.one_notMem_rad","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L94-L100","doc":"The radical is **proper**: normalisation `tr 1 = 1` keeps `1` out of it, so\nthe trace is never degenerate in the trivial direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.not_isFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.not_isFaithful","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L90-L92","doc":"A nonzero radical element **refutes** faithfulness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.isFaithful_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.isFaithful_iff","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L85-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.IsFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.IsFaithful","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L82-L83","doc":"**Faithfulness**: the trace form is nondegenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mul_mem_rad_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mul_mem_rad_left","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L75-L80","doc":"`rad` is a **left** ideal — this is where the trace property is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mul_mem_rad_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mul_mem_rad_right","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L71-L73","doc":"`rad` is a **right** ideal — by associativity alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mem_rad_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.mem_rad_iff","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.rad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceRadical.rad","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceRadical.lean#L59-L67","doc":"**The radical of the trace form** `⟨a, b⟩ = tr (a * b)`: the elements the\nform cannot see. ","signatureChunk":0}]}